////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Acid Test: Set Builder Chains Absent
//
// Splicing a chain condition into its trios says what the set builder
// notation denotes, so processSetBuilderChains() is unconditional: it
// consults neither the SetBuilderRule nor the ChainsRule, and with
// neither in the document the two spellings of a condition list still
// produce the same LC and so share a propositional atom.
//
// What is missing without the SetBuilderRule is the membership
// inference itself, in either direction.

Declare ∈, ≤

➤ "no rules: the spellings still share an atom"
{
  Declare m1, n1
  Assume n1 in set(k in ℤ : m1 ≤ k ≤ n1)
  n1 in set(k in ℤ : m1 ≤ k, k ≤ n1) ✔︎
}

➤ "no SetBuilderRule: neither direction of membership fires"
{
  Declare m2, n2
  {
    Assume n2 in set(k in ℤ : m2 ≤ k ≤ n2)
    m2 ≤ n2 ✗
  }
  {
    Assume m2 ≤ n2
    n2 in set(k in ℤ : m2 ≤ k ≤ n2) ✗
  }
}
